title: A parked thread survives the day boundary (Phase 10.6)
story: character-acceptance
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: Park the thread mid-beat with an off-thread ask, cross the
  day boundary in the Archive (scene close AND story-state turn), and
  resume - the resuming line renders and the next beat picks up at the
  held cursor.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/character-acceptance/chord/p10-threads.story
    stories/character-acceptance/tests/transcripts/p10-park-across-day.transcript

---

# Open the thread: beat 1.
> ask prompter about the shortfall
[OK: contains "It began with a missing shilling."]

# The off-thread ask parks the thread (passive default) and serves its topic.
> ask prompter about the ledger
[OK: contains "The ledger keeps its own counsel."]

# Cross the day boundary - the story state turns in the Archive.
> north
[OK: contains "morning finds you among the shelves"]

> south
[OK: contains "Counting Room"]

# The parked thread resumes across the closed scene and the turned day.
> ask prompter about the shortfall
[OK: contains "As I was saying about the shortfall."]

# The cursor held: the next prompt serves beat 2, not beat 1 again.
> continue
[OK: contains "Then a missing pound, and nobody blinked."]
